        <p class="lead">
          I am Lee Potter, an aquatic biogeochemist studying how phosphorus and carbon move through watersheds, sediments, and shallow estuarine systems. My work focuses on nutrient loading, internal sediment release, harmful algal bloom risk, and management-relevant water quality dynamics in the Lake Pontchartrain Basin and connected coastal environments.
