        <h2 class="section-heading">How nutrient biogeochemistry works</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          Biogeochemistry examines how chemical elements move through biological and physical components of Earth systems. In aquatic environments, nutrients such as phosphorus cycle between sediments, water, and organisms. Processes like microbial mineralization, redox reactions, sediment diffusion, and physical disturbance can release nutrients back into the water column, where they may stimulate primary production or harmful algal blooms.
        </p>

