      <h2 class="section-heading">Current themes</h2>
      <div class="themes">
        <div class="card theme-card">
          <h3>Legacy phosphorus in river sediments</h3>
          <p>Examining how redox conditions, dredging, and sediment age influence phosphorus release from subtropical tributaries flowing into the Lake Pontchartrain estuary.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card theme-card">
          <h3>Shear stress and internal loading</h3>
          <p>Evaluating how wind-driven sediment disturbance can mobilize bioavailable phosphorus and contribute to eutrophic conditions and harmful algal blooms in shallow estuarine systems.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card theme-card">
          <h3>Watershed-to-estuary nutrient pathways</h3>
          <p>Linking watershed loading, sediment storage, and coastal response using field data, long-term records, and geospatial analysis to support water quality management.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
